WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.139
He’s been called “The world’s most repulsive
politician.”

00:00:03.139 --> 00:00:08.860
His controversial statements have been described
as sexist, homophobic, and racist.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.919
His Government’s recent attempts to alter
data related to the coronavirus have lent

00:00:12.919 --> 00:00:18.180
credibility to those who had previously called
him “authoritarian.”

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:23.150
All of these criticisms and more had already
been leveled at Jair Bolsonaro before late

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:28.070
2018, when he won the Brazilian presidential
election in a landslide.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.500
So how did he do it?

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:37.780
Bolsonaro has made a career of having this
personality that's this very alpha male, macho,

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:43.590
"I'm going to show you," refusing to bow down
to critics kind of attitude.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:47.800
A lot of people make the comparison to Bolsonaro's
rise to the rise of Trump

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.240
In a broad brush kind of way

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.400
that is a totally fair comparison.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.500
It was a populist movement that swept Bolsonaro
into office, and it was a rejection of the

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:03.260
status quo... "and so that's an honor to give that to you"

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:07.460
Even if apt, however, the comparison may not
give Bolsonaro’s own electoral success enough

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.460
credit.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:12.900
Whereas Donald Trump won the US election while
losing the popular vote, Bolsonaro was elected

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:16.460
with around 55% of the vote in the final round

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.520
Unfortunately for him, that popularity
stands in stark contrast to today.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.750
He now faces an economic crisis, cratering
poll numbers, and a coronavirus outbreak that

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.720
is the worst in the region.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:33.880
The question now is whether Bolsonaro can
leverage his outspoken style and army of dedicated

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:38.210
supporters to salvage his presidency.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:42.420
Bolsonaro grew up with five brothers in the
Southern Brazilian town of Eldorado.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:48.259
After 2 years in Rio De Janeiro City Council,
he began his 27 year career in congress, and

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:50.100
his ascent to national fame.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:54.220
During this time, he would cement some of
his beliefs in the public eye.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:59.479
On crime, he said in 2017 “a policeman who
doesn’t kill isn’t a policeman.”

00:01:59.479 --> 00:02:05.659
On LGBT rights, he said in 2011 “No father
is capable of loving a gay son” He told

00:02:05.659 --> 00:02:10.470
fellow member of Congress 
that he “would not rape her, she is too

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:11.470
ugly.”

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:16.700
In July of 2018, he announced his candidacy
for President with the slogan “Brazil Above

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.540
Everything, God Above Everyone.”

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:23.790
He proved immediately adept at building an
unprecedented coalition of voters.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:31.340
So, that grouping of the alpha male, firearm
ownership, the evangelical, and then the military,

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.520
that has become his base.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.319
And they didn't used to be together.

00:02:34.319 --> 00:02:40.660
So, he's truly transformed the landscape of
Brazilian politics in a way that, it's hard

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.010
to see that going away.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:47.660
Bolsonaro also picked the perfect time to
portray himself as the anti-corruption candidate.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:52.840
Operation Car Wash, the largest anti-corruption
effort in Brazil’s history had begun only

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.100
a few years before, and had since ensnared
many important figures in the country’s

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.849
political left, including two former Brazilian presidents.

00:02:59.849 --> 00:03:03.650
Bolsonaro
took office as the 38th President of Brazil

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.700
at the beginning of 2019.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:11.230
He immediately made good on one campaign promise,
stripping Brazil’s indigenous affairs agency

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:15.650
of the responsibility to identify and demarcate
indigenous lands.

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:20.269
Indigenous people in Brazil
for several decades have been really aggressively

00:03:20.269 --> 00:03:24.460
pushing to get legal rights to their land
and title.

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:29.180
He specifically said when he was running for
election, that if he was elected he would

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:33.900
not allow indigenous people to get any more
land in Brazil and basically would shut down

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:34.989
all of those processes.

00:03:34.989 --> 00:03:40.970
That was the first thing he did when he came
into office, which is a very symbolic way

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:44.150
to indicate what your position is.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:49.459
When the Amazon experienced record-breaking
wildfires in mid-2019, Bolsonaro downplayed

00:03:49.459 --> 00:03:53.989
the damage, calling the data lies and firing
the head of the government organization that

00:03:53.989 --> 00:03:55.010
produced it.

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:59.459
After international outcry, he dispatched
soldiers and allocated funds to fight the

00:03:59.459 --> 00:04:00.459
fires.

00:04:00.459 --> 00:04:04.690
But Bolsonaro’s main focus, and what swept
him into office, was his promise to kickstart

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:06.590
Latin America’s largest economy.

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:13.450
...GDP in Bolsonaro’s first year in office
grew at only 1.1 percent, down from 1.3 percent

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:16.120
in each of the previous two years.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:20.639
His signature accomplishment so far has been
a pension reform bill that was passed with

00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:21.969
Congressional approval.

00:04:21.969 --> 00:04:26.660
He’s also spent his time in office stoking
increasingly larger fights with the press.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:38.140
the relationship with the media
is really antagonistic, in a way that hasn't

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:43.659
been seen before, and at a temperature level
that hasn't been seen before.

00:04:43.659 --> 00:04:47.970
Simone Iglesias: Bolsonaro stimulates his
supporters to fight with journalists.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:55.039
And every day it's the escalation of problems
and aggressivity in front of his residence.

00:04:55.039 --> 00:05:00.960
And because of that, all important TV channels
and newspapers suspend this coverage

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.399
because it became too aggressive.

00:05:03.399 --> 00:05:06.680
Now Bolsonaro faces a host of problems threatening
his administration.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:13.419
he has created a political crisis
on top of a public health crisis and a looming

00:05:13.419 --> 00:05:14.740
economic crisis.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:19.969
Most economists forecast that Latin America
is headed into a terrible scenario for the

00:05:19.969 --> 00:05:21.529
next year, possibly the next decade.

00:05:21.529 --> 00:05:25.619
he has multiplied the crises by pushing people

00:05:25.619 --> 00:05:28.360
out of his own government, out of his own
cabinet

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:33.000
Brazil has one of the highest death tolls
of any nation from coronavirus, and on many

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.199
days has the most confirmed new cases of any
country in the world.

00:05:37.199 --> 00:05:40.219
Bolsonaro 
has refused to endorse social distancing and

00:05:40.219 --> 00:05:44.180
expressed enthusiasm for using chloroquine
to treat the virus.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:48.580
In early June, Bolsonaro’s government was
accused of trying to cover up data related

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:53.919
to the coronavirus when the health ministry
pulled the entire historic database for Covid-19

00:05:53.919 --> 00:05:55.059
from its website

00:05:55.059 --> 00:05:59.809
The ministry has since relented and republished
some historical information amid a growing

00:05:59.809 --> 00:06:02.790
backlash
The President has downplayed the threat of

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:07.770
the virus, calling it “just a little flu”
and very infrequently dons a mask.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:13.699
The president in Brazil doesn't have power
to lock down and forbid the shops

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:15.420
and commerce here.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:21.700
But, the example of Bolsonaro is really strong. Thousands of people follow Bolsonaro.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:26.300
And when he said, "it's unnecessary
to use mask" for example-

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:28.999
Thousands of people follow.

00:06:28.999 --> 00:06:33.929
But even putting aside his handling of Brazil’s
Coronavirus outbreak, another threat looms

00:06:33.929 --> 00:06:37.639
in the resignation of Bolsonaro’s justice
minister, Sergio Moro.

00:06:37.639 --> 00:06:42.559
Moro is a national hero in Brazil, having
been the head investigative judge for Operation

00:06:42.559 --> 00:06:43.559
Car Wash.

00:06:43.559 --> 00:06:51.800
Flash forward to Moro resigning, and in his
resignation claiming the reason he was resigning

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:55.229
was because of corrupt practices of the President.

00:06:55.229 --> 00:06:58.259
That's totally damning to the credibility
of Bolsonaro.

00:06:58.259 --> 00:07:05.770
the short version is that Moro said that
he caught Bolsonaro trying to pressure him

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:11.580
to change the head of the Police Chief of
Rio de Janeiro and the head of police for

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:12.620
the federal government.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:17.770
Moro believes the reason Bolsonaro was pushing
to make those changes is because Bolsonaro’s

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:25.149
own children, his three sons, are under investigation
for criminal acts in Rio de Janeiro and at

00:07:25.149 --> 00:07:26.149
the federal level.

00:07:26.149 --> 00:07:31.149
Moro and Bolsonaro have declined to comment
for this video, and Bolsonaro and his sons

00:07:31.149 --> 00:07:35.139
have separately denied any wrongdoing in the
matter.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:40.460
Regardless, Bolsonaro’s approval rating
has taken a hit in light of the recent scandals,

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.700
his supporters love him.

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:49.679
There are diehard Bolsonaro fans in Brazil.

00:07:49.679 --> 00:07:57.099
They truly believe that the media
is attacking him, that all of the criticisms

00:07:57.099 --> 00:08:01.399
are just trying to bring down the only guy
who is trying to get rid of the corruption

00:08:01.399 --> 00:08:04.809
that Brazil has been riddled with for the
past several decades.

